---
import Legal from "../../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { useTranslations } from "../../i18n/utils";

const lang = "en";
const t = useTranslations(lang);
---

<Legal
	lang={lang}
	routeKey="privacy"
	title={t("meta.privacy.title")}
	description={t("meta.privacy.description")}
	heading="Privacy Policy"
>
	<p class="muted">
		This is a translation for convenience. The legally binding version is the
		German <a href="/datenschutz/">Datenschutzerklärung</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>1. Controller</h2>
	<p>
		The controller responsible for data processing on this website is:<br />
		Tim Schulz<br />
		Email: <a href="mailto:kontakt@timschulz.net">kontakt@timschulz.net</a>
	</p>

	<h2>2. General information on data processing</h2>
	<p>
		This website is implemented as a static site. No cookies are set and no
		cross-device or cross-site tracking takes place. For reach measurement, only
		a privacy-friendly, cookieless web analytics service is used (see section 4).
	</p>

	<h2>3. Hosting and server log files</h2>
	<p>
		This website is hosted by Vercel Inc., 340 S Lemon Ave #4133, Walnut, CA
		91789, USA ("Vercel"). When you access the site, Vercel, acting as a
		processor, handles technically necessary access data (server log files) that
		your browser transmits automatically:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>IP address of the accessing device</li>
		<li>date and time of access</li>
		<li>page / file requested</li>
		<li>browser and operating system used</li>
		<li>referrer URL</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		The legal basis is Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR. The legitimate interest lies in the
		technically error-free, secure and performant provision of the website. A
		data processing agreement pursuant to Art. 28 GDPR is in place with Vercel.
	</p>
	<p>
		Vercel is a provider based in the USA, so personal data (in particular the IP
		address) may be transferred to the USA. This transfer is safeguarded by the
		EU Standard Contractual Clauses (Art. 46 GDPR) and, where Vercel is certified
		accordingly, by the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework. For more information, see
		Vercel's privacy policy: <a
			href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy"
			target="_blank"
			rel="noopener noreferrer">vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy</a
		>.
	</p>

	<h2>4. Web analytics (Vercel Web Analytics)</h2>
	<p>
		To analyse access statistics, I use Vercel Web Analytics, a service provided
		by Vercel Inc. (address see above). The service is cookieless and works
		without persistent identifiers: no cookies are set and no information is
		stored on or read from your device. It does not identify individuals and does
		not track across devices or websites.
	</p>
	<p>
		Only aggregated data is collected, such as pages visited, referrer,
		approximate location (country), device type, operating system and browser. To
		distinguish visits, a non-reversible hash is generated from technical
		characteristics of the request and is discarded after at most 24 hours.
	</p>
	<p>
		The legal basis is Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR; the legitimate interest lies in the
		statistical analysis and improvement of the website. As Vercel is based in
		the USA, the notes on data transfer in section 3 apply accordingly. More
		information: <a
			href="https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/privacy-and-compliance"
			target="_blank"
			rel="noopener noreferrer"
			>vercel.com/docs/analytics/privacy-and-compliance</a
		>.
	</p>

	<h2>5. Fonts</h2>
	<p>
		The fonts used (Fira Mono and Fira Sans) are served locally from my own
		server. There is <strong>no</strong> connection to third-party servers (such
		as Google Fonts), and no personal data is transferred to third parties in the
		process.
	</p>

	<h2>6. Contact by email</h2>
	<p>
		If you contact me by email, your details (email address, message content) are
		stored in order to process your request. The legal basis is Art. 6 (1) (b)
		and (f) GDPR. The data is deleted as soon as it is no longer required to
		fulfil its purpose.
	</p>

	<h2>7. External links and social networks</h2>
	<p>
		This website links to external profiles (GitHub, LinkedIn, YouTube,
		Instagram). These are simple links; no content from these providers is
		embedded. Only when you click a link are you forwarded to the respective
		platform, whose privacy policy then applies.
	</p>

	<h2>8. Your rights</h2>
	<p>You have the right at any time to:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>access to the data stored about you (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
		<li>rectification of inaccurate data (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
		<li>erasure (Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
		<li>restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
		<li>data portability (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
		<li>object to processing (Art. 21 GDPR)</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection
		supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR).
	</p>

	<h2>9. SSL/TLS encryption</h2>
	<p>
		For security reasons, this site uses SSL/TLS encryption. You can recognise an
		encrypted connection by the "https://" in your browser's address bar.
	</p>
</Legal>
